SWEET AUDIO EP1 SERVICE (patch 0181, plan A12), on top of 0180: boot-arg sweetaoc=15 (with sweetamp=1). Run a10h found that the AOC sends
PCM to TDM0 only from entry point EP1 (audio_playback1, BIND2 src 1 -> SINK_SPEAKER, S16 fixed PLAYBACK), not from EP0. This level makes
the 0173 /dev/sweetaudio service use that path: the 0176 HAL amp words, the 0172 power-up (DSP firmware, RESUME, GLOBAL_EN), then the AOC
switched to EP1 with the a10h probe-10 setup (no tone), the DAC on ASPRX1 (DSP bypassed, as the audible a10h replay) and the 0177 detector
(DSP1 RX3/RX4 on ASPRX1, CSPL_TEMPERATURE) read in silence and in self-test beep 1. The feed keeps at most 6 KiB (32 ms) queued ahead of the
AOC reader and jumps to the reader if it ever falls behind (resync count). Kernel self-test: 2 beeps 1 kHz at -16 dBFS. The amps are powered
down in the stock order after 30 s without a writer and powered up again on the next open (amp SPI only around power-up / power-down, plus
one detector read per open within 4 s). Shutdown / remote reset: the stop hook waits <= 1 s for the stock power-down. Gain clamp (user
decision 2026-11-18): default -15 dB, max -6 dB. Also fixes the restore race on pad gpp23 (amp R reset bit 7 and touch chip select bit 3 in
one DAT word): the amp pad read-modify-writes and the touch tg_pin_put / tg_pin_set_func take one spin lock (sweet_pad_spin).
Levels <= 14 unchanged except the gain clamp and the pad lock. USER DECISION 2026-11-18: speed first, no mutants.

